<body><div class=WordSection1>
<p class=inst>Sardar Vallabhbhai National Institute of Technology (SVNIT), Surat</p>
<p class=dept>Department of Artificial Intelligence</p>
<p class=course>Agentic AI (IA462) &mdash; Semester VIII</p>
<hr>
<table class=g><tr><th>Name</th><th>Roll No.</th><th>Experiment</th><th>Date</th></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>U23AI042</td><td>7</td><td>31 October 2026</td></tr></table>
<h1>Experiment 7</h1>
<h1 class=sub>Agent Behaviour as a Markov Decision Process &mdash; Value and Policy Iteration</h1>
<h2>Aim</h2>
<p>To model an agent acting in a stochastic environment as a Markov Decision Process (MDP), compute the optimal value function and policy by Value Iteration, obtain the same policy by Policy Iteration from an arbitrary starting policy, and compare the two methods by the computational work each performs.</p>
<h2>Theory</h2>
<p>An MDP formulates an agent's sequential decision-making problem as a 5-tuple &lang;<i>S</i>, <i>A</i>, <i>P</i>, <i>R</i>, &gamma;&rang;: a set of states <i>S</i>, a set of actions <i>A</i> available in each, a transition probability function <i>P</i>(<i>s</i>'|<i>s</i>,<i>a</i>), a reward function <i>R</i>(<i>s</i>,<i>a</i>,<i>s</i>'), and a temporal discount factor &gamma; &in; [0, 1). Because of the Markov property, the optimal behavior is fully described by a stationary policy &pi;: <i>S</i> &rarr; <i>A</i>, and the value of a state <i>V</i><sup>&pi;</sup>(<i>s</i>) represents the expected cumulative discounted future return.</p>
<p>The <b>Bellman Optimality Equation</b> expresses the recursive relationship for optimal values:</p>
<p class=eq><i>V</i>*(<i>s</i>) = max<sub><i>a</i> &in; <i>A</i></sub> &sum;<sub><i>s</i>'</sub> <i>P</i>(<i>s</i>' | <i>s</i>, <i>a</i>) [ <i>R</i>(<i>s</i>, <i>a</i>, <i>s</i>') + &gamma; <i>V</i>*(<i>s</i>') ]</p>
<p>Two dynamic programming algorithms compute this solution:</p>
<ul><li><b>Value Iteration</b>: Turns the Bellman optimality equation directly into an update operator, sweeping repeatedly across all non-terminal states until max<sub><i>s</i></sub> |<i>V</i><sub><i>k</i>+1</sub>(<i>s</i>) &minus; <i>V</i><sub><i>k</i></sub>(<i>s</i>)| &lt; tol, extracting the greedy policy once at convergence.</li><li><b>Policy Iteration</b>: Alternates between exact <i>Policy Evaluation</i> (solving or iterating to find <i>V</i><sup>&pi;</sup>) and <i>Policy Improvement</i> (updating &pi;(<i>s</i>) &larr; argmax<sub><i>a</i></sub> <i>Q</i>(<i>s</i>,<i>a</i>)). It terminates when policy changes cease (&pi;<sub><i>k</i>+1</sub> = &pi;<sub><i>k</i></sub>).</li></ul>
<p class=cap>Table 1. The GridWorld Environment Specification.</p>
<table class=g><tr><th style='width:22%'>Element</th><th style='width:78%'>Specification</th></tr><tr><td>States</td><td>4 columns &times; 3 rows (11 states total); cell (1, 1) is a barrier/wall and not a state.</td></tr><tr><td>Terminals</td><td>Goal at (3, 2) with reward +1.0; Trap at (3, 1) with reward &minus;1.0.</td></tr><tr><td>Actions</td><td>up, down, left, right available in all 9 non-terminal states.</td></tr><tr><td>Transitions</td><td>Intended move with probability 1 &minus; 2p; perpendicular slips each with probability p. Bumping into walls or boundaries keeps the agent in place.</td></tr><tr><td>Parameters</td><td>Default slip probability p = 0.1, step reward R<sub>step</sub> = &minus;0.04, discount factor &gamma; = 0.95, start state (0, 0).</td></tr></table>
<h2>Algorithm</h2>
<h3>Algorithm 1 &mdash; Value Iteration</h3>
<ol><li>Initialize <i>V</i>(<i>s</i>) = 0 for all non-terminal states <i>s</i> &in; <i>S</i>. Set tolerance tol = 10<sup>&minus;6</sup>.</li><li>For each sweep <i>k</i> = 1, 2, ...: compute for every non-terminal state <i>Q</i>(<i>s</i>, <i>a</i>) = &sum;<sub><i>s</i>'</sub> <i>P</i>(<i>s</i>'|<i>s</i>,<i>a</i>)[<i>R</i> + &gamma;<i>V</i>(<i>s</i>')], and set <i>V</i><sub>new</sub>(<i>s</i>) = max<sub><i>a</i></sub> <i>Q</i>(<i>s</i>, <i>a</i>).</li><li>Check convergence &Delta; = max<sub><i>s</i></sub> |<i>V</i><sub>new</sub>(<i>s</i>) &minus; <i>V</i>(<i>s</i>)|. If &Delta; &lt; tol, terminate.</li><li>Extract optimal policy &pi;*(<i>s</i>) = argmax<sub><i>a</i></sub> <i>Q</i>(<i>s</i>, <i>a</i>).</li></ol>
<h3>Algorithm 2 &mdash; Policy Iteration</h3>
<ol><li>Initialize an arbitrary policy &pi;<sub>0</sub>(<i>s</i>) = 'up' for all non-terminal states, and values <i>V</i>(<i>s</i>) = 0.</li><li><b>Policy Evaluation</b>: Sweep <i>V</i><sub><i>k</i>+1</sub>(<i>s</i>) &larr; <i>Q</i>(<i>s</i>, &pi;(<i>s</i>), <i>V</i><sub><i>k</i></sub>) until values settle within tolerance tol. Record evaluation sweeps and updates.</li><li><b>Policy Improvement</b>: For each state, find greedy action <i>a</i>* = argmax<sub><i>a</i></sub> <i>Q</i>(<i>s</i>, <i>a</i>, <i>V</i>). If <i>a</i>* &ne; &pi;(<i>s</i>), set &pi;(<i>s</i>) &larr; <i>a</i>* and mark policy unstable.</li><li>If policy is unchanged across all states, terminate; otherwise, repeat evaluation.</li></ol>
<h2>Source Code (exp7_mdp.py)</h2>
<pre class=code style='font-size:7.0pt'>&quot;&quot;&quot;SVNIT Surat — Department of Artificial Intelligence
Agentic AI (IA462) — Semester VIII
Experiment 7: Agent Behaviour as a Markov Decision Process — Value and Policy Iteration
Roll No: U23AI042
&quot;&quot;&quot;

import os
import numpy as np

# ── 1. Environment &amp; MDP Formulation ──
ACTIONS = [&quot;up&quot;, &quot;down&quot;, &quot;left&quot;, &quot;right&quot;]
DELTAS = {&quot;up&quot;: (0, 1), &quot;down&quot;: (0, -1), &quot;left&quot;: (-1, 0), &quot;right&quot;: (1, 0)}
PERP = {
    &quot;up&quot;: [&quot;left&quot;, &quot;right&quot;],
    &quot;down&quot;: [&quot;left&quot;, &quot;right&quot;],
    &quot;left&quot;: [&quot;down&quot;, &quot;up&quot;],
    &quot;right&quot;: [&quot;down&quot;, &quot;up&quot;],
}
WALL = (1, 1)
TERMINALS = {(3, 2): 1.0, (3, 1): -1.0}
STATES = [(c, r) for c in range(4) for r in range(3) if (c, r) != WALL]
NON_TERMINALS = [s for s in STATES if s not in TERMINALS]

def get_next_cell(s, a):
    dc, dr = DELTAS[a]
    nc, nr = s[0] + dc, s[1] + dr
    if 0 &lt;= nc &lt; 4 and 0 &lt;= nr &lt; 3 and (nc, nr) != WALL:
        return (nc, nr)
    return s

def transitions(s, a, p=0.1):
    prob_map = {}
    ns = get_next_cell(s, a)
    prob_map[ns] = prob_map.get(ns, 0.0) + (1.0 - 2 * p)
    for pa in PERP[a]:
        pns = get_next_cell(s, pa)
        prob_map[pns] = prob_map.get(pns, 0.0) + p
    return list(prob_map.items())

def q_value(s, a, V, step_r=-0.04, gamma=0.95, p=0.1):
    q = 0.0
    for ns, prob in transitions(s, a, p):
        r = TERMINALS[ns] if ns in TERMINALS else step_r
        v_next = 0.0 if ns in TERMINALS else V[ns]
        q += prob * (r + gamma * v_next)
    return q

def value_iteration(step_r=-0.04, gamma=0.95, p=0.1, tol=1e-6):
    V = {s: 0.0 for s in NON_TERMINALS}
    sweeps = 0
    while True:
        delta = 0.0
        new_V = {}
        for s in NON_TERMINALS:
            best_q = max(q_value(s, a, V, step_r, gamma, p) for a in ACTIONS)
            delta = max(delta, abs(best_q - V[s]))
            new_V[s] = best_q
        V = new_V
        sweeps += 1
        if delta &lt; tol:
            break
    policy = {
        s: max(ACTIONS, key=lambda a: q_value(s, a, V, step_r, gamma, p))
        for s in NON_TERMINALS
    }
    return V, policy, sweeps

def policy_iteration(step_r=-0.04, gamma=0.95, p=0.1, tol=1e-6):
    pi = {s: &quot;up&quot; for s in NON_TERMINALS}
    V = {s: 0.0 for s in NON_TERMINALS}
    rounds = 0
    total_eval_sweeps = 0
    total_updates = 0
    while True:
        rounds += 1
        while True:
            delta = 0.0
            new_V = {}
            for s in NON_TERMINALS:
                v_new = q_value(s, pi[s], V, step_r, gamma, p)
                delta = max(delta, abs(v_new - V[s]))
                new_V[s] = v_new
                total_updates += 1
            V = new_V
            total_eval_sweeps += 1
            if delta &lt; tol:
                break
        policy_stable = True
        for s in NON_TERMINALS:
            old_a = pi[s]
            best_a = max(ACTIONS, key=lambda a: q_value(s, a, V, step_r, gamma, p))
            if best_a != old_a:
                policy_stable = False
                pi[s] = best_a
        if policy_stable:
            break
    return V, pi, rounds, total_eval_sweeps, total_updates

def display_grid(V, pi=None, title=&quot;&quot;):
    print(f&quot;\n{&#x27;=&#x27;*30} {title} {&#x27;=&#x27;*30}&quot;)
    ARROWS = {&quot;up&quot;: &quot;  ^  &quot;, &quot;down&quot;: &quot;  v  &quot;, &quot;left&quot;: &quot;  &lt;  &quot;, &quot;right&quot;: &quot;  &gt;  &quot;}
    for r in reversed(range(3)):
        val_row = []
        act_row = []
        for c in range(4):
            s = (c, r)
            if s == WALL:
                val_row.append(&quot;  WALL  &quot;)
                act_row.append(&quot;  WALL  &quot;)
            elif s in TERMINALS:
                val_row.append(f&quot; {TERMINALS[s]:+6.2f} &quot;)
                act_row.append(f&quot;  {TERMINALS[s]:+1.0f}   &quot;)
            else:
                val_row.append(f&quot; {V[s]:6.4f} &quot;)
                act_row.append(ARROWS[pi[s]] if pi else &quot;   .  &quot;)
        print(f&quot;Row {r}: |&quot; + &quot;|&quot;.join(val_row) + &quot;|    |&quot; + &quot;|&quot;.join(act_row) + &quot;|&quot;)

def compute_absorption_prob(pi, p):
    s_idx = {s: i for i, s in enumerate(NON_TERMINALS)}
    n = len(NON_TERMINALS)
    Q = np.zeros((n, n))
    R_neg = np.zeros(n)
    for s in NON_TERMINALS:
        i = s_idx[s]
        a = pi[s]
        for ns, prob in transitions(s, a, p):
            if ns == (3, 1):
                R_neg[i] += prob
            elif ns in NON_TERMINALS:
                Q[i, s_idx[ns]] += prob
    P_fail = np.linalg.solve(np.eye(n) - Q, R_neg)
    return P_fail[s_idx[(0, 0)]]

if __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:
    all_valid = all(
        abs(sum(prob for _, prob in transitions(s, a)) - 1.0) &lt; 1e-9
        for s in NON_TERMINALS for a in ACTIONS
    )
    print(f&quot;MDP Initialized: {len(STATES)} states ({len(NON_TERMINALS)} non-terminal, {len(TERMINALS)} terminal).&quot;)
    print(f&quot;All transition probability distributions sum to 1.0: {all_valid}&quot;)

    # Value Iteration
    V_vi, pi_vi, vi_sweeps = value_iteration()
    display_grid(V_vi, pi_vi, &quot;Value Iteration Converged Values &amp; Policy&quot;)
    print(f&quot;\nSweeps to convergence: {vi_sweeps}&quot;)
    print(f&quot;Total value updates:   {vi_sweeps * len(NON_TERMINALS)} ({vi_sweeps} sweeps x {len(NON_TERMINALS)} states)&quot;)
    print(f&quot;Start state V(0, 0):   {V_vi[(0, 0)]:.4f}&quot;)

    # Policy Iteration
    V_pi, pi_pi, pi_rounds, pi_eval_sweeps, pi_updates = policy_iteration()
    display_grid(V_pi, pi_pi, &quot;Policy Iteration Converged Values &amp; Policy&quot;)
    print(f&quot;\nImprovement rounds:        {pi_rounds}&quot;)
    print(f&quot;Total evaluation sweeps:   {pi_eval_sweeps}&quot;)
    print(f&quot;Total value updates:       {pi_updates}&quot;)
    print(f&quot;Start state V(0, 0):       {V_pi[(0, 0)]:.4f}&quot;)

    # Verification
    max_diff = max(abs(V_vi[s] - V_pi[s]) for s in NON_TERMINALS)
    policy_agreement = all(pi_vi[s] == pi_pi[s] for s in NON_TERMINALS)
    print(f&quot;\n--- Verification with Algorithm 1 ---&quot;)
    print(f&quot;Policies agree across all states: {policy_agreement}&quot;)
    print(f&quot;Maximum difference in state values: {max_diff:.2e} (&lt; tolerance 1e-6)&quot;)

    # Exercise 1: Step reward sweep
    print(&quot;\n&quot; + &quot;=&quot; * 80)
    print(&quot;EXERCISE 1A: STEP REWARD SWEEP (gamma = 0.95, p = 0.1)&quot;)
    print(&quot;=&quot; * 80)
    for r in [-0.01, -0.04, -0.1, -0.5, -2.0]:
        V, pi, sw = value_iteration(step_r=r, gamma=0.95, p=0.1)
        print(f&quot;R_step = {r:+5.2f} | V(0,0) = {V[(0,0)]:+7.4f} | Sweeps = {sw:2d}&quot;)
        print(f&quot;  Policy: Row 2={[pi[(c,2)] for c in range(3)]} | Row 1={[pi[(0,1)], pi[(2,1)]]} | Row 0={[pi[(c,0)] for c in range(4)]}&quot;)

    # Exercise 1: Discount factor sweep
    print(&quot;\n&quot; + &quot;=&quot; * 80)
    print(&quot;EXERCISE 1B: DISCOUNT FACTOR SWEEP (R_step = -0.04, p = 0.1)&quot;)
    print(&quot;=&quot; * 80)
    for g in [0.5, 0.7, 0.9, 0.95, 0.99]:
        V, pi, sw = value_iteration(step_r=-0.04, gamma=g, p=0.1)
        print(f&quot;gamma  = {g:5.2f} | V(0,0) = {V[(0,0)]:+7.4f} | Sweeps = {sw:2d}&quot;)
        print(f&quot;  Policy: Row 2={[pi[(c,2)] for c in range(3)]} | Row 1={[pi[(0,1)], pi[(2,1)]]} | Row 0={[pi[(c,0)] for c in range(4)]}&quot;)

    # Exercise 2: Slip sweep
    print(&quot;\n&quot; + &quot;=&quot; * 80)
    print(&quot;EXERCISE 2: SLIP PROBABILITY SWEEP (R_step = -0.04, gamma = 0.95)&quot;)
    print(&quot;=&quot; * 80)
    for p in [0.0, 0.05, 0.1, 0.2, 0.3]:
        V, pi, sw = value_iteration(step_r=-0.04, gamma=0.95, p=p)
        prob_neg = compute_absorption_prob(pi, p)
        print(f&quot;p = {p:4.2f} | V(0,0) = {V[(0,0)]:+7.4f} | Sweeps = {sw:2d} | P(reach -1) = {prob_neg:7.4f}&quot;)
        print(f&quot;  Policy: Row 2={[pi[(c,2)] for c in range(3)]} | Row 1={[pi[(0,1)], pi[(2,1)]]} | Row 0={[pi[(c,0)] for c in range(4)]}&quot;)</pre>
<h2>Procedure and Results</h2>
<p>The program was executed in the SVNIT Agentic AI laboratory environment. Below is the complete captured trace of Value Iteration, Policy Iteration, algorithm verification, and parameter sweep outputs.</p>
